>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_frac_type`

``` hol4
Refute.register_frac_type :
  {tyop : {Thy : string, Tyop : string},
   ersatz :
     {original : {Thy : string, Name : string},
      replacement : {Thy : string, Name : string}} list} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers a nullary fraction-like type and its model-finder replacements.

`tyop` names an existing nullary HOL type.  Each `ersatz` row names an
existing original constant and the existing constant used in its place by
model-finder preprocessing.  Original keys in the list must be distinct.
Active fraction mappings have precedence over ordinary ersatz mappings.

The operation validates the complete registration before changing
session state, then atomically replaces any fraction registration for the
same type operator.  It also removes any quotient or typedef registry row
for that operator, because the explicit fraction classification supersedes
it.  It does not create a HOL type, constant, or theorem.

### Failure

Fails if the type does not exist or is not nullary, an ersatz constant
does not exist, original keys repeat, or the operator is an interpreted,
free datatype, or codatatype classification.

### See also

[`Refute.register_frac_type_rat`](#Refute.register_frac_type_rat),
[`Refute.register_frac_type_real`](#Refute.register_frac_type_real),
[`Refute.register_ersatz`](#Refute.register_ersatz),
[`Refute.register_term_postprocessor`](#Refute.register_term_postprocessor),
[`Refute.register_quotient`](#Refute.register_quotient),
[`Refute.register_typedef`](#Refute.register_typedef)

Fraction encoding is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
